0,Romani music - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romani_music,"The Romani community has significantly influenced flamenco, jazz manouche, Russian ‘romances’, Balkan music, Hungarian czardas, and various fusions with jazz, hip-hop, Western art music, and various folk genres across Europe.","Romani, Balkan",Indo-European
1,Romani people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romani_people,"The Romani language is an Indo-Aryan language with strong Persian, Armenian, Greek, and South Slavic influence.[104][105][106][107] Balkan Romani also shows an extensive Turkish influence.[108] It is divided into several dialects...","Romani, Balkan",Indo-European
2,Music - RomArchive,https://www.romarchive.eu/en/music/,"In this section we give a brief sampling of musicians for whom jazz training was paramount. Balkan Romani music has gone global. Few people are aware, however, of the multitude of different styles played by Roma from this region. RomArchive has selected some examples to highlight this diversity.","Romani, Balkan",Indo-European
