4,Romani music — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/Romani_music,"Romani musicians entered Europe in significant numbers during the 15th century, following migrations from the Byzantine and Ottoman territories, where they had already adapted performance practices to local contexts.","Romani, Balkan",Indo-European
5,Balkan Gypsy Music - YouTubeThe Balkan Hour - Balkan Romani Music - YouTube MusicBalkan - RomArchive,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KJEUxVGQIuk,"Romani music or Gipsy music is the music of the Romani people, who have their origins in northern India, but today live mostly in Europe. Historically nomadi... This is a collection of Romani / Roma / Gypsy music. Its meant to show the diversity of Romani music while also allowing people to recognize how each country creates an imprint on the style... Balkan Romani music has gone global. Few people are aware, however, of the multitude of different styles played by Roma from this region. RomArchive has selected some examples to highlight this diversity.","Romani, Balkan",Indo-European
6,The Balkan Hour - Balkan Romani Music - YouTube Music,https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLF63FBE90C22DD18D,This is a collection of Romani / Roma / Gypsy music. Its meant to show the diversity of Romani music while also allowing people to recognize how each country creates an imprint on the style...,"Romani, Balkan",Indo-European
7,Balkan - RomArchive,https://www.romarchive.eu/en/music/balkan/,"Balkan Romani music has gone global. Few people are aware, however, of the multitude of different styles played by Roma from this region. RomArchive has selected some examples to highlight this diversity.","Romani, Balkan",Indo-European
8,Balkan Romani — Wikipedia Republished // WIKI 2,https://web.archive.org/web/20200824113856/https://wiki2.org/en/Balkan_Romani,"Classification. Indo-European, Indo-Iranian, Indo-Aryan, Intermediate Divisions, Western, Romani, Balkan. History. Most of the people who speak Balkan Romani are Romani themselves. Another meaning of the prefix rom is someone belonging to the Romani ethnicity.","Romani, Balkan",Indo-European
9,Balkan Romani – TIPs,https://tips.translation.bible/tip_language/rmn/,"Balkan Romani (rmn) is a(n) Indo-European language of Albania, Austria, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Bulgaria, Belarus, Switzerland, Czechia, Germany, Finland, France, United Kingdom, Greece, Croatia, Hungary, Iran, Islamic Republic of, Italy, Lithuania, Latvia, Moldova, Republic of...","Romani, Balkan",Indo-European
